    "done_when": "A second live-service reach from the test suite, measured by a peer session (report: ~/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/lanes-stamp-leak.md). In an environment whose codex home can answer, mcp_views.crew_lanes_view called without a probe_reader spawns the real `codex app-server` account probe: reckon/_backends.py probe_budget, around line 3274, then run_probe, around line 3333. The lane is then dated by the live observation instead of the record stamp. The peer reproduced tests/test_preflight_pace.py's stamp red with CODEX_HOME set and green without, in one process. Where codex cannot answer, each probe costs about 20 s instead. Either way, a test's outcome and runtime depend on the machine's live account. A peer node is fixing only tests/test_preflight_pace.py by injecting a no-answer reader. This node closes the class.\n\n1. In tests/conftest.py, add an autouse fixture beside no_live_jev so that no test spawns a real provider account probe. Replace reckon._backends.run_probe, or the narrowest seam that launches the external account probe, with a stub that raises a named error stating that live account probes are disabled under test, or that returns the existing \"no answer\" result; choose whichever keeps the callers' documented no-answer path working. Tests that exercise probe behaviour with their own fake binary or reader must keep working: let a test opt in through a marker or by patching the seam itself, as the Jev guard allows. List in the evidence every test file that newly needed to opt in.\n2. Add tests/test_suite_never_probes_live_accounts.py. With CODEX_HOME pointed at a fake home that would answer, call crew_lanes_view with no probe_reader and assert that no subprocess is spawned (spy subprocess.Popen and run), and that the lane carries the record stamp. Removing the guard must make this fail; that is your negative control.\n3. Measure: run tests/test_preflight_pace.py and any test file that reaches probe_budget, with the guard and without it, recording wall time and pass/fail in docs/evidence/fragments/one-typesafe-model-picker/suite-never-probes-live-accounts.html.\n\nGate: the new file, tests/test_preflight_pace.py, tests/test_suite_never_calls_live_jev.py, tests/test_budget*.py and tests/test_backends*.py if present. Run them with the main checkout's .venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -n 8 in the FOREGROUND, with one log for base and one for head under the run directory, each ending in an EXIT line, judged by delta. Do not edit reckon/_backends.py unless a seam is missing; if one is, add the smallest injection point and say so.",
